# downloads.phext — the pin register

Will's rule (2026-11-22): "we don't have to validate the
remote end beyond having an expected hash and source, if no
hash is known, we log the first occurrence in downloads.phext
and track that in exo-plan." Companion rule, same exchange:
"just always audit the inputs to a job" — "no unexpected
inputs allowed." A job's inputs are declared in advance and
the set is closed; an artifact that arrives hash-less gets
its first occurrence pinned here (hash + source), and every
later occurrence must match the pin. A mismatch is an
unexpected input — a defect that stops the job.

Seeded: 2026-11-22, at Will's direction: "seed it now with every download you're aware of." Sweep scope: MEMORY.md, memory/2026-11-*.md, workspace registers and goal workspaces, and live node state (fleet NFS share on orchid-flow, node partials) hashed on-node 2026-11-22.

Evidence grades (one per entry, mandatory):
- FULL — sha256 + size + source all from primary evidence or
  computed live.
- PARTIAL — some of hash/size/source missing; the entry names
  which.
- RECORD-ONLY — mentioned in records, no artifact locatable.

Entries: 34
By grade: FULL 17, PARTIAL 13, RECORD-ONLY 4
By status: active 24, partial 6, removed 1, exiled 3

Coordinate scheme: this Home scroll at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1; one
scroll per download at 1.1.1/1.1.2/1.1.<n>, n the entry's
sequence number in (first-occurrence date, name) order. The
builder (~/workspace/phext/build_downloads_phext.py)
documents the scheme and its renumbering caveat in full; the
source of truth is ~/workspace/phext/downloads-source.json.

